; subtotal_posts (--subtotal, period reports, equity) keeps real, virtual
; (parenthesized) and balanced virtual (bracketed) postings to one account
; apart, keyed by (account name, virtual, must balance).  Its old key, the
; account name with a 0x01 byte appended for any virtual posting, put (A)
; and [A] in one entry that took the flags of whichever came first, so the
; bracketed 1 DDD below printed as (Assets:Broker), dropped out of the
; equity total and left a spurious Opening Balances line.

2024/01/05 Buy
    Assets:Broker    10 AAA
    Assets:Broker    5 BBB
    Assets:Cash     $-100.00
    Equity:Start

2024/01/06 Budget
    (Assets:Broker)    3 AAA
    (Assets:Broker)    2 CCC
    [Assets:Broker]    1 DDD
    [Equity:Start]    -1 DDD

test equity
2024/01/06 Opening Balances
    Assets:Broker                             10 AAA
    Assets:Broker                              5 BBB
    (Assets:Broker)                            3 AAA
    (Assets:Broker)                            2 CCC
    [Assets:Broker]                            1 DDD
    Assets:Cash                             $-100.00
    Equity:Start                             $100.00
    Equity:Start                             -10 AAA
    Equity:Start                              -5 BBB
    [Equity:Start]                            -1 DDD
end test

test reg -s -F '%(display_account)|%(display_amount)\n'
Assets:Broker|10 AAA
5 BBB
(Assets:Broker)|3 AAA
2 CCC
[Assets:Broker]|1 DDD
Assets:Cash|$-100.00
Equity:Start|$100.00
-10 AAA
-5 BBB
[Equity:Start]|-1 DDD
end test
